<span class="pn-normal"><b>Traveller:</b> figures we would have a patch today, i was going to Lguk to do some side quests.<br><b>Malken:</b> You can believe them both I guess. I'm technically online since I'm logged in to the site and I have my browser up but then I'm not really online since I wasn't actively looking at the tab for the site <img src="../pnimages/smilies/icon_smile.gif"    border="0" /><br><b>Shalara:</b> Ok, I'm confused.  The sidebar says that Malken is on-line, the main page says he is not.  Which one do I belive?<br><b>Shalara:</b> Ok, it's 9:30 AM - what are you two doing on at this hour? <img src="../pnimages/smilies/icon_smile.gif"    border="0" /><br><b>Serenya:</b> Glad to hear they fixed things <img src="../pnimages/smilies/icon_smile.gif"    border="0" />  I love Adaware esp.<br><b>Shalara:</b> Looks like everything's back to normal now.  Thanks Mal/Shagg/Whatever <img src="../pnimages/smilies/icon_smile.gif"    border="0" /><br><b>Shalara:</b> Malken, I need you to log in please<br><b>Kedrith:</b> Ahh Thats a good upgrade then.<br><b>Malken:</b> Not this time, we actually asked for it. Upgraded to a 1.5M down / 384 K up from a 384/384 and it costs half as much and we got rid of the SBC phone line that had been dedicated to DSL. <img src="../pnimages/smilies/icon_smile.gif"    border="0" /><br><b>Kedrith:</b> Ahhh dont you hate it when they "upgrade" your stuff that was working fine in the first place and then it gets all messed up?</span>

